MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Owner-reported, validated on production before touching code: the Stamp
tool drew 'a rectangle with the word approved above it', the Image stamp
button was 'not clickable', and Squiggly 'just highlighted text'. All
three were the editor misrepresenting a file that was already right —
Annotate's raster is deliberately clean, so the overlay is the only
rendering anyone sees, and it painted every markup kind as a highlight
wash, every stamp as a bare outline with a floating name badge, and the
image-stamp entry sat natively disabled with its answer in a tooltip.

The overlay now draws each mark the file's own way: wash / line under /
line through / wave under for the four markups (OverlayItem.quadStyle);
bordered squeezed capitals for stamps (stampText, camel-case split like
MuPDF's own appearance); the uploaded pixels for image stamps
(imageUrl, stretched to the rect exactly as the appearance stream is),
with a stamp-style IMAGE placeholder once only the file holds them. The
image-stamp palette entry is always pressable — with no stamp it opens
the picker whose file arms it (contract §3 amended; supersedes the
2026-08-23 'disabled until' spec). strokePx scales by the page's own
width, not A4's.

Behind the report, two engine defects, probed with PyMuPDF before
fixing: add_stamp_annot aspect-fits /Rect to the built-in appearance
(a 3:2 drag saved as ~4:1, image pixels squashed into the reshaped
box), and annot.update() writes the stamp's name over the user's
/Contents comment. Both stamp branches now restore the drawn rect and
the typed comment as RAW xref writes (rect × ~transformation_matrix,
probed equal to set_rect on /Rotate 0/90/180 and offset-CropBox pages)
— raw because set_rect/set_info mark the annot dirty and MuPDF
re-synthesises dirty stamps when a later op loads another page, which
un-did the restore mid-batch.

Unit 608/67 files (6 new); engine+annotations-API 505 passed; ruff,
mypy, ng lint clean; build + 43 prerender + verify:prerender green;
new-frontend-vs-production-API harness pass in both themes, console
clean (evidence in docs/reviews/evidence/annotate-defects/). The two
phase-3 e2e cases (amended stamp flow, new truth test) have not run
anywhere yet — the CLI gate proves them.

